10
00:40:54,545 --> 00:41:00,545
Despicable Me 3 is a 2017 American animated comedy film directed by Pierre
Coffin and Kyle Balda and written by Cinco Paul and Ken Daurio.

11
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Produced by Illumination, it is the fourth feature
film in the Despicable Me franchise.

12
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
The film stars the voices of Steve Carell (in a dual role), Kristen Wiig, Trey Parker, Coffin,
Miranda Cosgrove, Steve Coogan, Jenny Slate, Dana Gaier, Nev Scharrel and Julie Andrews.

13
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
In the film, Gru teams up with his long-lost twin brother Dru to stop Balthazar Bratt, a former child
actor of the 1980s, from destroying Hollywood after his show was canceled years ago.

14
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
Development on a third main Despicable Me film began in 2013
with Coffin returning as director alongside Balda.

15
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
The film was in the early writing stages by 2014,
while the cast was announced in 2016.

16
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Heitor Pereira and Pharrell Williams returned to compose the score.

17
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
Despicable Me 3 debuted at the Annecy International Animated Film Festival on June 14, 2017, and
was theatrically released in the United States on June 30, by Universal Pictures.

18
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
It received mixed reviews from critics, and grossed $1.035 billion worldwide, becoming the fourth-highest-grossing
film of 2017 and the fourth-highest-grossing animated film of all time during its theatrical run.

19
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
A further sequel, Despicable Me 4, was released in 2024.

20
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
The film explores themes of prison, villain, twin brother, sequel, jail.

21
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The tone is lighthearted.
